n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tWed\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t4\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tDecember 4, 2024 @ 10:00 am - December 21, 2024 @ 2:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tLOBBY EXHIBITION Salt Spring Groove – A Photographic Collection of Salt Spring Musicians\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tArtSpring - Lobby\t\n\t\n\t\t100 Jackson Avenue, Salt Spring Island, BC, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tAs a music photographer, my goal is to capture the excitement, passion, and intensity of live performance. These candid images reveal the soul of the performers, showing them at their best—how they want to be seen and remembered. For the audience, the photographs become a part of the experience, a way to relive the magic […]\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tNovember 2024\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tSat\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t2\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tNovember 2, 2024 @ 10:00 am - November 30, 2024 @ 4:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tSS Foundation: 40 Years of Giving — In Pictures\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tArtSpring - Lobby\t\n\t\n\t\t100 Jackson Avenue, Salt Spring Island, BC, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t40 Years of Giving – In Pictures celebrates the diverse impact of Salt Spring Island Foundation-funded community projects over the past four decades. Through striking imagery, the exhibit highlights the Foundation’s commitment to the following nine key funding areas: Arts & Culture Children and Youth Seniors Belonging, Equity & Reconciliation Poverty Relief & Economy Housing, […]\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tOctober 2024\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tTue\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t1\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tOctober 1, 2024 @ 10:00 am - October 31, 2024 @ 2:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tLobby Exhibition: League 181 “Working Together”\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tArtSpring - Lobby\t\n\t\n\t\t100 Jackson Avenue, Salt Spring Island, BC, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tLeague 181 was established in 2013 by a small group of experienced painters with a compact of mutual help, learning and development.  The central idea is that we benefit by painting together in a group, both by discussion of the craft and by observation of each other. We have pleasure in presenting a selection of […]\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tSeptember 2024\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tFri\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t13\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\tFeatured\n\t\n\t\tSeptember 13, 2024 @ 3:00 pm - 5:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tMAKANA YOUTH CHOIRS: Fall Term\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tArtSpring - Lobby\t\n\t\n\t\t100 Jackson Avenue, Salt Spring Island, BC, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tFridays, Sep 13-Nov 24 |The Makana Choirs are the place to develop healthy singing habits, learn musical literary skills, and put on a concert. All while having fun with friends! Makana is directed by Caroni Young and accompanied by Cicela Månsson. ++ The Makana Kids Class is for singers in grades 2-5. This class is […]\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$145 – $165\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tTue\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t3\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tSeptember 3, 2024 @ 10:00 am - September 30, 2024 @ 4:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tLobby Exhibition: Diverse Threads\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tArtSpring - Lobby\t\n\t\n\t\t100 Jackson Avenue, Salt Spring Island, BC, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tThe Island Textile Artists latest show called \"Diverse Threads\" reflects the multitude of ways in which working with textiles creates pleasing and exciting art. Our group of nine members is very diverse. Some of us prefer hand stitching, others prefer machine stitching while some like to do gel prints or manipulate fabric with a heat […]\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tJuly 2024\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tTue\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t16\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tJuly 16, 2024 @ 10:00 am - August 30, 2024 @ 2:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tLobby Exhibition: Megan Coupland\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tArtSpring - Lobby\t\n\t\n\t\t100 Jackson Avenue, Salt Spring Island, BC, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\"Making Lemonade\" It began in 2020, all three boys home all the time. I make the food offerings to appease them, array myself in the ragged vestments of my order and undertake the pilgrimage through my garden to the sacred ancient trailer that holds the tools of my faith. I complete the ritual choosing of […]\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tJune 2024\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tTue\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t4\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tJune 4, 2024 @ 10:00 am - June 28, 2024 @ 2:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tLobby Exhibition: Sherry Leigh Williams & Patricia Rose Williams, with Sheena Gering\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tArtSpring - Lobby\t\n\t\n\t\t100 Jackson Avenue, Salt Spring Island, BC, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tNew Event! Meet the Artists FRIDAY JUNE 21 | 10am-2pm Sherry Leigh Williams and Sheena Gering are hosting a \"Meet the Artist\" drop-in event within the Lobby Gallery space to conduct walk-and-talks about the work and their Métis culture, engage and answer questions, and Sheena will be conducting a beading and felted tufting demonstration. Live jazz […]\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\tPrevious Events\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\tToday\t\n\n\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tNext Events\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\t\n\n\t\n\n\n